**Definition 4.1 (one-run counters and ordered stencil).** At a native
cut let $C$ count all constructed tape cells, including original and
added boundaries, the meter, all old banks/code/copies/dead material;
let $c$ count present finite locations among $q$, and let $\ell$ count
actual installed head links. At row $i$ use the following lists, evaluated
on its actual pre-row state, with no independently optimized fragment.

The ordered cell-role list $\mathcal D_i$ contains core operands and
neighbors, every actual finite-effect marker role in written order, then
the old meter append cell. Repeated identities remain repeated inspections.
The append-site list $\mathcal A_i$ is core then receipt. The old-graph
head-slot probe list $\mathcal J_{i,\mathrm{old}}$ is in port/lane order;
each word includes its final slot probe. New endpoint initialization is
an assignment, not an old-graph probe. The fresh finite-socket list is
$\mathcal Z_i$. Its route ends at the actual absent socket. Let $d_r$
be the root-to-finite-component length and $\pi_x$ the corresponding
specified root route. The probe prescription is

$$
\begin{aligned}
p_i={}&d_r+6q+3c_{i-1}-4
 +\sum_{x\in\mathcal D_i}(|\pi_x|+68)\\
 &+\sum_{z\in\mathcal A_i}(|\pi_z|+2)
 +\sum_{w\in\mathcal J_{i,\mathrm{old}}}|w|
 +\sum_{z\in\mathcal Z_i}(|\pi_z|+2).
\end{aligned}
$$

Let $e_i$ count actual core-plus-receipt cell births, $s_i$ fresh finite
bits, $t_i$ distinct designated existing native-bit targets after alias
combination, $r_i$ head retargets and $a_i$ first activations. Include
PC/token/control targets in $t_i$ but not the freshly constructed bit.
Prescribed no-op targets remain charged. The actual finite-effect list
determines $t_i,\mathcal D_i$; an old fixed-three-cell estimate is not
used for arbitrary raw CTLs. These lists instantiate SSA/CSA's stencil
method at 74 roles; their literal 64-role constants are not transferred.

